<title>USA: International Remote Imaging 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>International Remote Imaging 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>CHATSWORTH, Calif. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year Ended Dec. 31	     1996	    1995</p>
<p>			  Net sales	 $20,554,131   $14,392,158</p>
<p>			    Earnings (loss) (7,428,188)   2,126,412</p>
<p>	     Earnings (loss) per share	(1.21)	    .33</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding   6,141,657    6,418,518</p>
<p>NOTE: The loss in 1996 was due primarily to more than $7.5 million in acquisition and merger expenses, and $1.8 million of other unusual non-recurring charges connected with the company's decision not to pursue a public offering, recently completed litigation and arbitration matters, as well as severance and other related costs stemming from the operational restructuring and downsizing of its workforce during the fourth quarter.</p>
</text>
